    <color name="ic_launcher_background">@color/md_theme_surface</color>
    <!-- The logo triad — see values/colors.xml for the roles and the history.
         Dark theme differs from light in one structural way that matters:
         the CONTAINER tones here are genuinely DARK (tone ~30) under LIGHT
         on-colours, which is what M3 expects and what this palette previously
         did NOT do. It used to copy the light-theme relationship into night —
         secondaryContainer #FAB186 at L* 78, a LIGHT fill under a DARK
         on-colour — and that is a real defect, not a stylistic one:
           · a container-toned control landed at 10.04:1 against the #131315
             page while the primary CTA beside it was 6.44:1, so a mode
             selector out-shouted the button it feeds (the buy screen);
           · the home backup pill's GRACE state paints a hardcoded amber
             (#e8a13d) as its ink, which on the old light fill was 1.18:1 —
             invisible. On the dark container below it is 4.61:1.
         Every live consumer of these tokens is a paired fill+ink (bg_sync_code
         in two layouts, the home backup pill, and chip_download which is
         remapped away by ThemeOverlay.App.Chip), so the inversion was audited
         consumer by consumer before being made. Re-do that audit before
         touching them again — a consumer that pairs one of these with a
         HARDCODED ink is what an inversion breaks. -->
    <color name="md_theme_primary">#ff716c</color>
    <color name="md_theme_onPrimary">#460005</color>
    <!-- NOT retoned, ever — the hero FAB. See values/colors.xml. -->
    <color name="md_theme_primaryContainer">#F66A66</color>
    <color name="md_theme_onPrimaryContainer">#0F0000</color>
    <!-- The CONTROL ACCENT — coral, not the triad's peach. See
         values/colors.xml: bare platform widgets resolve their tint through
         this token, so a peach here paints the indeterminate spinners peach in
         dark theme and dark brown in light. -->
    <color name="md_theme_secondary">#ff716c</color>
    <color name="md_theme_onSecondary">#460005</color>
